{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity and internal consistency review of the entire patent application draft, including all claims, the detailed description, the figure briefs, and the list of reference numerals. Every limitation in every claim, every numbered part, and every specific structure, relationship, and variant described in the application text and figure briefs was traced to an exact affirmative passage in the inventor's disclosure and conversation files.\n\nThe review identified one critical disclosure-fidelity issue. The figure briefs and drawing descriptions introduce a specific, unsupported physical path for the mechanical indicator stem, showing it crossing the air circulation passages. The inventor's disclosure requires only that the stem be thermally coupled to a phase-change cassette, not that it follow this particular path. This unsupported detail has been documented in a finding with a specific fix to remove the unsupported language from the text, which will in turn drive the regeneration of the corresponding figure geometry to be source-faithful.\n\nWith the exception of this finding, the remainder of the application text was found to be fully supported by the inventor's source materials and internally consistent. The terminology is used consistently, all numbered parts are correctly identified and described, and no drafting notes or placeholders remain. The claims are progressively narrowed in a supported ladder of dependent claims. The optional nature of the wick and indicator features is correctly stated and supported. The final summary and findings are provided in the structured output."}
